    "brand": "Thorne",
    "badge": "Best Certified Whey",
    "category": "NSF Certified for Sport whey isolate",
    "description": "Thorne's isolate pairs a short ingredient list with NSF Certified for Sport status, per Thorne and NSF at the time of writing, which covers label-claim checks and contaminant screening as well as banned substances. A scoop of about 28 g gives 21 g of protein in roughly 100 calories, with about 2-3 g of sugar depending on flavor, per the label. Whey isolate tends to test lower for heavy metals than plant proteins.",
    "pros": [
